//! Entries slice — Batch 190 (Plan 187 / Research 222) — the cubecl #1731
//! umax-divisor pack of 1: the compiler-enabling source clamp that admits
//! LLVM LSR past a runtime unsigned divisor in address math.
//!
//! Source: `tracel-ai/cubecl` @ `30a7ef00cd56e72716130b7111f2cfaa8664664d`
//! (PR #1731, "fix(llvm): clamp unsigned divisors so LSR can reduce
//! addresses behind them", `SamuelBelanger`, 2026-09-29; MIT OR Apache-2.0
//! dual). Clone was `.raw/` ephemeral — deleted after this batch committed;
//! every load-bearing quote was re-verified VERBATIM at the pin (commit
//! message + the three diff hunks: the `insert_umax_one` lowering, the
//! `strided_walk` kernel, the PTX `a_strided_walk_advances_its_address`
//! regression test).
//!
//! Graded at the 09-30 01:5x item-11 pass (B+ candidate from the commit
//! message); this slot's diff re-verification CONFIRMED the mechanism and
//! found the fix is at the COMPILER-LOWERING level (all cubecl-llvm
//! UDivOp/URemOp lowerings clamp the rhs; SDiv/SRem deliberately untouched
//! — the unsigned-only contract is load-bearing and rides the rule).
//!
//! Category: O (IR strength reduction) — the family's first RUNTIME-divisor
//! member (the existing four are the constant pow2 shift family). The
//! fixture models the EMITTED shape on both sides, exactly like the
//! source's own PTX assertion (no `mad.lo`/`mul.lo` in the loop body);
//! fixtures are ORIGINAL minimal reproductions, never pasted source.

use super::KernelRule;

pub fn entries() -> Vec<KernelRule> {
    vec![
        // ── O: an unsigned div/rem by a RUNTIME value becomes a udiv in
        // scalar evolution; LSR only expands a udiv whose divisor it can
        // prove non-zero. An address whose loop-invariant start holds one
        // (a cube position split by a launch-time count) was left rebuilt
        // from the loop counter EVERY iteration. ─────────────────────────
        KernelRule {
            rule_id: "clamp-runtime-divisor-for-lsr-address-reduction".to_string(),
            gpu_concept: "MECHANISM (compiler-enabling source clamp): an unsigned division or remainder by a RUNTIME value becomes a udiv/urem in scalar evolution, and LLVM's loop strength reduction only expands a udiv whose divisor it can PROVE non-zero — so an address whose loop-invariant start holds one (a cube position split by a count known only at launch: `(pos_y % bands) * pitch`, `pos / count` tile-index splits) was left rebuilt from the loop counter on every iteration instead of advancing as an add-recurrence in registers. The cost is SCHEDULING, not arithmetic: in a matmul reading its weight along K, ptxas then issued 3 of the loop's 9 loads before the first FFMA instead of all 9, and the loop waited on memory several times per iteration (the dependent address multiply sits on each load's critical path). FIX (one source-level op): divide by `umax(rhs, 1)` — non-zero-ness becomes provable (umax with 1 is >= 1), LSR expands the division, and the address registers advance by an ADD per iteration so the scheduler can hoist every load ahead of the compute. THREE CONTRACT HALVES: (1) a CONSTANT divisor folds the clamp away at compile time (umax(c, 1) = c for c >= 1 — zero cost on the constant paths the O-family's shift rules already own); (2) div-by-zero semantics ALIGN with WGSL by the same clamp — 'Division by zero was undefined in LLVM, and now gives what WGSL defines: x / 0 = x, x % 0 = 0' (a/1 = a, a%1 = 0 reproduce WGSL exactly), so on GPU targets the clamp is a semantic FIX, not merely an optimization; (3) UNSIGNED ONLY — the source lowering clamps UDivOp/URemOp and deliberately leaves SDivOp/SRemOp untouched (umax does not bound a SIGNED value away from zero; signed div-by-zero has no WGSL-aligned clamp), so a signed runtime divisor keeps a hard divide or needs its own host-side non-zero contract. REGIME: unsigned div/rem by a launch-time/runtime value (band count, pitch, tile divisor, position split) feeding ADDRESS or index math inside a hot loop, on LLVM-backed targets (NVPTX, SPIR-V, AMDGPU) where LSR runs over the generated IR. ANTI-REGIME: constant divisors (already folded — strength-reduce-div/mod-pow2 territory, and the clamp is dead code the compiler removes); divisions outside address recurrences (a one-off udiv costs nothing to leave); compilers that do not run LSR over div (hand-write the magic — shader-fastdiv-mulhi is that lane); float-reciprocal-able scalars (pack-scalar-params' host inv_dim lane — integer INDEX math cannot take a float reciprocal without breaking exactness, which is why this lane exists at all); divisors already guarded to >= 1 at the host layer (the clamp is then a free no-op proof, harmless but redundant). NOT-BENCHABLE here: no validator in this corpus hosts a ptxas/SASS scheduling metric — lands as decision content (the Batch-136 shape); the measured-GOAT offer rides the lane-intel note (any of our CubeCL/MSL/CUDA kernels dividing by a launch-time count in address math — tile-index/position splits — re-measures before adoption). VERIFICATION DISCIPLINE (the source's own regression test — pin the CODEGEN, never the timing): assert on the ASSEMBLY that the loop body contains no address multiply (`!body.contains(\"mad.lo\") && !body.contains(\"mul.lo\")` over the first-label-to-back-edge slice) — a compiler-scheduling property is pinned by the artifact it produces, never by a benchmark that could pass for other reasons. KINSHIP (do not double-count): strength-reduce-div-pow2 / strength-reduce-mod-pow2 = the CONSTANT-divisor arm of this same family (x/2^k -> shift; the clamp is the family's RUNTIME-divisor generalization — a constant divisor folds the clamp into exactly those rules); shader-fastdiv-mulhi = the HAND-WRITTEN magic-division cluster for shaders (host-precomputed magic pairs + mulhi intrinsics + the fastdiv_small zero-guard); this rule delegates the SAME magic expansion to the compiler by making the divisor provably non-zero — prefer the clamp wherever the compiler runs LSR, fall to fastdiv where it does not; division-by-invariant-multiplication (rust_perf B59) = the CPU hand-rolled libdivide form (same family, hand-vs-compiler axis, CPU-vs-GPU substrate); hoist-bit-address-out-of-packed-row-sweep = LICM of an address decomposition whose DIVIDEND is loop-invariant (hoist the whole div/mod out of the loop); here the address ADVANCES with the loop counter — there is nothing to hoist, the recurrence is what must reduce (the two compose: hoist what is invariant, clamp-reduce what advances); pack-scalar-params-into-combined-buffer = hoists the reciprocal to the HOST for float scalars (inv_dim precomputed once) — exact integer indexing cannot take that lane; predicate-gated-skip-empty-workset-step = count >= 1 guaranteed at the HOST layer by batch elision (this guarantees it at the DIV SITE for the compiler's benefit — different layer, the same count-never-zero instinct); base-3-trit-packing's div/mod decode = CONSTANT divisors in decode (already compiler-reduced; its 'div/mod expensive on CUDA scalar ALU' regime note is the arithmetic-cost class, not this recurrence-blocking mechanism). CITE: tracel-ai/cubecl @ 30a7ef00c -- crates/cubecl-llvm/src/shared/to_llvm/math.rs (insert_umax_one + `lower_int_bin_arith!(UDivOp => llvm::UDivOp, insert_umax_one)` and the URemOp twin, with SDivOp/SRemOp deliberately unclamped) + crates/cubecl-llvm/src/shared/offline_kernels.rs (strided_walk: `(CUBE_POS_Y % bands) * pitch` — the runtime-divisor address start, 'how a matmul reads its weight along the reduced axis') + crates/cubecl-llvm/src/nvptx/offline_tests.rs (a_strided_walk_advances_its_address: no mad.lo/mul.lo in the PTX loop body) + the commit message (the 3-of-9 loads / waited-on-memory narrative + the WGSL div-by-zero alignment + the constant-fold note, quoted verbatim in Research 222), MIT OR Apache-2.0. Batch 190 / Plan 187 / Research 222.".to_string(),
            ref_shape: "// NAIVE: the address math divides by a RUNTIME value — the divisor\n// is a udiv/urem in scalar evolution that LSR cannot prove non-zero,\n// so LSR refuses to expand it and the address is left as a function\n// of the loop counter: REBUILT with an integer multiply on every\n// iteration, on each load's critical path. ptxas then issues 3 of the\n// loop's 9 loads before the first FFMA instead of all 9 — the loop\n// waits on memory several times per iteration.\npub fn walk_naive(w: &[f32], out: &mut [f32], bands: u32, pitch: u32, stride: u32, steps: u32) {\n    // runtime-divisor urem in the address's loop-invariant START —\n    // `bands` is only known at launch, SCEV cannot prove it non-zero\n    let start = (pos_y() % bands) * pitch;\n    let mut sum = 0.0f32;\n    for s in 0..steps {\n        let row = s * 32 + unit_pos_x();\n        // the address is rebuilt from the counter EVERY iteration — the\n        // mul (a mad.lo in PTX) sits on the load's critical path\n        let addr = (row * stride + start) as usize;\n        sum += w[addr];\n    }\n    out[abs_pos()] = sum;\n}\n\nfn pos_y() -> u32 {\n    0\n}\nfn unit_pos_x() -> u32 {\n    0\n}\nfn abs_pos() -> usize {\n    0\n}".to_string(),
            opt_pattern: "// OPT: divide by umax(rhs, 1) — the divisor becomes provably non-zero,\n// LSR expands the udiv/urem, and the address advances as an add-\n// recurrence: an ADD per iteration, no mul, no div in the loop body —\n// every load issues ahead of the compute (9 of 9). A constant divisor\n// folds the clamp away; x/0 becomes WGSL's x/0 = x, x%0 = 0 (was LLVM\n// UB) — on GPU targets the clamp is a semantic fix, not just a win.\npub fn walk_clamped(w: &[f32], out: &mut [f32], bands_in: u32, pitch: u32, stride: u32, steps: u32) {\n    let bands = bands_in.max(1); // umax(rhs, 1): the non-zero PROOF\n    let start = (pos_y() % bands) * pitch; // expandable now (divisor >= 1)\n    // the reduced form LSR emits: base + s * (32 * stride) — the mulhi\n    // magic folds into the induction, the address register advances by\n    // an ADD (the PTX regression test pins exactly this: no mad.lo, no\n    // mul.lo in the loop body)\n    let base = unit_pos_x() as usize * stride as usize + start as usize;\n    let advance = 32usize * stride as usize; // the constant addrec step\n    let mut addr = base;\n    let mut sum = 0.0f32;\n    for _ in 0..steps {\n        sum += w[addr];\n        addr += advance; // ADD per iteration — loads hoist ahead of FFMAs\n    }\n    out[abs_pos()] = sum;\n}\n\nfn pos_y() -> u32 {\n    0\n}\nfn unit_pos_x() -> u32 {\n    0\n}\nfn abs_pos() -> usize {\n    0\n}".to_string(),
        },
    ]
}
